note[lint.prefer-env-path-list]: `PATH` is extended by formatting a `:`-separated string
  /laputa/pm/execute.xsh:166:11
      PATH: f"{build_root}/bin:{build_root}/usr/bin:{e"PATH" ?? ""}",
            -------------------------------------------------------- a `List[Path]` environment value joins its entries and keeps their bytes
note: as a list this value differs in three cases: when `PATH` is unset there is no trailing empty entry, which a search reads as the current directory; bytes that are not UTF-8, in `PATH` or in an interpolated Path, are kept; and an entry that contains `:` fails instead of becoming two entries
help: write the search path as a list (apply manually: see the note for what changes) -> [fp"{build_root}/bin", fp"{build_root}/usr/bin", @env.PathList.PATH ?? []]
